Verification on 28 October 2026: `cargo check --locked -p lince-resources --features publication --tests` passed; the publication integration test in `crates/resources/tests/ergon.rs` passed. Lingua checks passed for Inquiry, STEM, and the updated register. A separate local-reference audit checked 1,140 targets across the new content and touched entrances/register, confirmed unique new or moved identities, and found no bundled source media. Run Cargo and Lingua through the repository's Nix environment.

The quantitative subject starts at arithmetic and extends through equations, functions, graphs, geometry, technical drawings, process accounting, uncertainty, similarity, sensitivity, and approximation. Metrology deepens into calibration design, traceability, physical influences, regression, uncertainty including correlation/nonlinearity/vector results, sampling, nine physical measurement families, comparison, conformity, laboratory competence, and independent research. Both use whole books and increasingly demanding studies. The wider subject scopes below remain pending even where an existing narrow trail or introductory Record can be reused.

