The three original inline programs ran in fresh Python 3.13.13 processes from a different working directory through Nix. The recycle/purge account matched independent exact five-unknown and three-unknown linear systems in 320 cases, including closure, physical limits, fresh-feed rescaling and rejected domains. The fixed-ratio flash matched an exact binary solution and independent 75-digit safeguarded Newton calculation in 349 cases: 220 two-phase, 64 liquid, 61 vapor and four indeterminate active-unity-ratio cases; normalization, component closure, equilibrium ratios, scaling/reordering, nonmutation and invalid-input rejection passed. The consecutive-reaction cascade matched independent exact three-equation stage systems in 500 cases, with positivity/conservation, zero/equal-rate limits, rejected inputs and first-order convergence to an independently derived plug-flow solution. Separate exact/Decimal checks verified teaching arithmetic, all three physical thermal steady states and full-Jacobian stability, the reversible air-separation bound and atom balances for 24 authored chemical equations.

