All three original inline programs ran in fresh Python 3.13.13 processes from another working directory. The two-bus AC calculation passed 3,000 cases against high-precision Decimal and an independent rectangular Newton formulation, including balance and the solvability boundary. The constrained three-bus dispatch passed 288 cases against exact rational nodal equations, active-boundary enumeration and convex optimization, with balance, feasibility and scaling checks. Its default now demonstrates a binding 0.2 line limit: generation 0.9/0.6, flows 0.2/0.8/0.7 and cost 1.53, compared with 1.0/0.5 and 1.50 after relaxing that limit. Exact fractions independently verify those teaching values. The fault-clearing swing calculation passed 274 cases against numerical equal-area roots, independent RK4 integration, second-order refinement, energy and time/inertia scaling. One hundred twenty-nine invalid domains were rejected and eleven additional teaching calculations passed. These bounded, explicitly normalized examples do not establish the validity of untested general solvers or physical installations.

